1
00:02:31,110 --> 00:02:36,110
This is the time known as the Great Pirate Era.

2
00:02:36,110 --> 00:02:39,110
A countless array of pirates go to battle across the seas

3
00:02:39,110 --> 00:02:41,110
in search of the One Piece,

4
00:02:41,110 --> 00:02:44,110
the legendary treasure left behind by Gold Roger,

5
00:02:44,110 --> 00:02:45,110
King of the Pirates.

6
00:02:45,110 --> 00:02:48,110
Monkey D. Luffy, a boy whose body turned to rubber

7
00:02:48,110 --> 00:02:50,110
after eating the gum gum fruit,

8
00:02:50,110 --> 00:02:53,110
set sail to become the next King of the Pirates.

9
00:02:53,110 --> 00:02:56,110
As Luffy and his crew conquer numerous obstacles,

10
00:02:56,110 --> 00:02:59,110
they capture the unwanted attention of the world government,

11
00:02:59,110 --> 00:03:02,110
which will use any means necessary to stop them.

12
00:03:02,110 --> 00:03:05,110
Now this is sight!

13
00:03:05,110 --> 00:03:08,110
Can't wait to see what kind of adventure's up next!

14
00:03:08,110 --> 00:03:12,110
With a charted course awash in danger and intrigue,

15
00:03:12,110 --> 00:03:17,110
the crew will cut a path across the Grand Line to the New World.

16
00:03:22,110 --> 00:03:24,110
Separated from the rest of his crew,

17
00:03:24,110 --> 00:03:28,110
Luffy has finally arrived at Marineford to rescue his brother Ace.

18
00:03:28,110 --> 00:03:32,110
He breaks into the plaza and eventually makes his way to the scaffold.

19
00:03:32,110 --> 00:03:35,110
There, with some unexpected help from an old enemy,

20
00:03:35,110 --> 00:03:37,110
Luffy finally frees Ace.

21
00:03:37,110 --> 00:03:43,110
Then, the brothers begin their escape as Whitebeard gives his sons a final order.

22
00:03:47,110 --> 00:03:51,110
Make no mistake! I'm a relic of a bygone era.

23
00:03:51,110 --> 00:03:53,110
Long have I sailed.

24
00:03:53,110 --> 00:03:56,110
But no ship can carry me into the new age.

25
00:04:03,110 --> 00:04:06,110
Let's finally put an end to this.

26
00:04:06,110 --> 00:04:12,110
The power that can burn even fire.

27
00:04:12,110 --> 00:04:14,110
Akainu's Ruthless Pursuit.

28
00:04:20,110 --> 00:04:22,110
The Marineford's falling apart!

29
00:04:22,110 --> 00:04:24,110
Somebody stop Whitebeard!

30
00:04:27,110 --> 00:04:30,110
Damn! At this rate, he's gonna bring down the whole island!

31
00:04:30,110 --> 00:04:40,110
We came here as a family! We should leave as one too!

32
00:04:40,110 --> 00:04:42,110
Yeah! Pops, come with us!

33
00:04:45,110 --> 00:04:48,110
You mean to disobey your captain's order?

34
00:04:48,110 --> 00:04:50,110
I told you fools to get away!

35
00:04:51,110 --> 00:04:52,110
Pops, no!

36
00:04:53,110 --> 00:04:55,110
All right! This might be our only chance!

37
00:04:55,110 --> 00:04:57,110
Hit Whitebeard with all you've got!

38
00:05:08,110 --> 00:05:09,110
I won't do it!

39
00:05:10,110 --> 00:05:13,110
Hey, come on, we're better off doing what Pops says.

40
00:05:13,110 --> 00:05:15,110
Are you crazy? Pops is our father!

41
00:05:15,110 --> 00:05:17,110
I won't leave him here to die!

42
00:05:17,110 --> 00:05:18,110
Let go!

43
00:05:18,110 --> 00:05:19,110
Don't be stupid!

44
00:05:19,110 --> 00:05:22,110
Do you think any of us want to leave Pops behind?

45
00:05:22,110 --> 00:05:23,110
Move!

46
00:05:23,110 --> 00:05:26,110
Bickering about your own petty feelings at a time like this,

47
00:05:26,110 --> 00:05:28,110
that's the kind of stuff Pops wouldn't stand for!

48
00:05:28,110 --> 00:05:31,110
Can't you see that he's trying to do what's best for us?

49
00:05:35,110 --> 00:05:36,110
Sorry.

50
00:05:41,110 --> 00:05:43,110
Everyone get back on the ships!

51
00:05:44,110 --> 00:05:45,110
Hey, Ace!

52
00:05:49,110 --> 00:06:03,110
Come on! Hurry it up! We're about to take off!

53
00:06:11,110 --> 00:06:13,110
Commander Marco, let's head back!

54
00:06:14,110 --> 00:06:15,110
Pops...

55
00:06:16,110 --> 00:06:21,110
You completely ruined the Navy's plan!

56
00:06:22,110 --> 00:06:23,110
Die!

57
00:06:23,110 --> 00:06:24,110
Don't kill me!

58
00:06:24,110 --> 00:06:26,110
I just want to leave this disaster!

59
00:06:26,110 --> 00:06:27,110
You don't have to do this!

60
00:06:28,110 --> 00:06:29,110
Sheen your sword!

61
00:06:30,110 --> 00:06:31,110
What the...?

62
00:06:32,110 --> 00:06:34,110
My exquisite wax shell is impenacrable!

63
00:06:35,110 --> 00:06:37,110
You will need more than a cheap blade to pierce this carapace!

64
00:06:38,110 --> 00:06:40,110
Dammit! More devil fruit powers!

65
00:06:40,110 --> 00:06:41,110
Figures!

66
00:06:41,110 --> 00:06:44,110
No wonder he was able to protect Fire Fist Ace on the scaffold!

67
00:06:44,110 --> 00:06:46,110
He even blocked Fleet Admiral Shingoku's attack!

68
00:06:47,110 --> 00:06:48,110
Oh, uh...

69
00:06:48,110 --> 00:06:50,110
Well, I wouldn't say I'm that powerful.

70
00:06:50,110 --> 00:06:52,110
My skill set is better suited for the arts.

71
00:06:55,110 --> 00:06:56,110
Thank you for your time!

72
00:06:56,110 --> 00:06:57,110
Time to mute!

73
00:07:06,110 --> 00:07:08,110
My fear! Unreal! He oughta be dead!

74
00:07:09,110 --> 00:07:11,110
What's it gonna take to put this guy away?!

75
00:07:11,110 --> 00:07:12,110
Go away!

76
00:07:14,110 --> 00:07:17,110
She no longer has to worry about saving Fire Fist Ace.

77
00:07:18,110 --> 00:07:19,110
Admiral, sir?

78
00:07:20,110 --> 00:07:24,110
So long as his men can escape, he'll sink Marineford and all of us with it.

79
00:07:25,110 --> 00:07:28,110
He's prepared to die. I've no doubt.

80
00:07:28,110 --> 00:07:33,110
Vice Admiral Garp! You okay?

81
00:07:34,110 --> 00:07:38,110
Whitebeard thinks our era is over?

82
00:07:39,110 --> 00:07:41,110
Yeah, the old man is probably right.

83
00:07:42,110 --> 00:07:44,110
We still don't know what happened to Whitebeard!

84
00:07:45,110 --> 00:07:48,110
What about his allies? Did he really sell them out or what?

85
00:07:49,110 --> 00:07:51,110
This block out's getting ridiculous!

86
00:07:52,110 --> 00:07:53,110
How long will we have to wait?

87
00:07:53,110 --> 00:07:58,110
If that stupid clown didn't block our view with that fat head of his,

88
00:07:59,110 --> 00:08:02,110
then maybe we'd have a clue what was actually going on!

89
00:08:04,110 --> 00:08:05,110
Is that who I think it is?

90
00:08:06,110 --> 00:08:09,110
Can it really be the renowned pirate Captain Buggy?

91
00:08:10,110 --> 00:08:11,110
Huh?

92
00:08:12,110 --> 00:08:14,110
I'm sorry, did someone say my name?

93
00:08:15,110 --> 00:08:17,110
Weird. So was he trying to tell us something?

94
00:08:18,110 --> 00:08:21,110
Perfect. How am I supposed to write a story on the battle now?

95
00:08:21,110 --> 00:08:24,110
What's wrong with their snails? We don't go it all day!

96
00:08:25,110 --> 00:08:26,110
Really?

97
00:08:27,110 --> 00:08:30,110
That piece of crap is still hiding in his shell?

98
00:08:31,110 --> 00:08:33,110
Come on! Get back out here, Mr. Snail!

99
00:08:34,110 --> 00:08:37,110
We still need your help! Captain Buggy's ready to defeat Whitebeard!

100
00:08:38,110 --> 00:08:39,110
Don't they realize what they're saying?

101
00:08:40,110 --> 00:08:42,110
Yeah, Whitebeard's wounded, but he's tearing down buildings!

102
00:08:43,110 --> 00:08:44,110
Just look at the bastard!

103
00:08:45,110 --> 00:08:47,110
Why'd I have to go and say I'd beat him?

104
00:08:47,110 --> 00:08:49,110
These morons believe anything you tell them!

105
00:08:50,110 --> 00:08:53,110
It's their fault for feeding my ego! I can't help it!

106
00:08:54,110 --> 00:08:58,110
Lure it out! We gotta showcase Captain Buggy's awesomeness for the entire world to see!

107
00:08:59,110 --> 00:09:01,110
Bring it over here! I'll just smash the shell open!

108
00:09:02,110 --> 00:09:04,110
Yeah! One strong pound ought to do it!

109
00:09:05,110 --> 00:09:06,110
No, stick your hand in there and yank!

110
00:09:07,110 --> 00:09:09,110
Let's soak it in salt water! Snails love that, right?

111
00:09:10,110 --> 00:09:11,110
Good idea! Let's do it!

112
00:09:12,110 --> 00:09:14,110
Quit messing with the poor thing, you bulls!

113
00:09:15,110 --> 00:09:16,110
Huh?

114
00:09:17,110 --> 00:09:22,110
Just think about it. It's not like he wants to be here slaving away from the Navy getting stuck in their battles and beaten up by guys like us.

115
00:09:23,110 --> 00:09:25,110
He's just trying to do his job in difficult times!

116
00:09:26,110 --> 00:09:29,110
Filming a war like this has gotta be traumatic, so relax and cut him some slack!

117
00:09:29,110 --> 00:09:36,110
No! How will you broadcast your plan? The Captain Buggy beats Whitebeard senseless as the entire world is watching live plan!

118
00:09:37,110 --> 00:09:42,110
Yeah, isn't that what you wanted? To stick it to the Navy and Whitebeard to prove that you're king of the pirates?

119
00:09:43,110 --> 00:09:44,110
I'm disappointed! Seriously, boss!

120
00:09:45,110 --> 00:09:52,110
Good grief! Sure they're loyal and stupid, but they're also a bunch of hard-ass prisoners who are locked up and impelled down!

121
00:09:52,110 --> 00:09:55,110
I better not piss them off too much!

122
00:09:56,110 --> 00:09:58,110
The transponder snail came out on his own!

123
00:09:59,110 --> 00:10:02,110
What? Is he... is he crying?

124
00:10:03,110 --> 00:10:07,110
It's a miracle! He must have been touched by Captain Buggy's kind words!

125
00:10:08,110 --> 00:10:13,110
Captain Buggy's compassion isn't lost on even the simplest of creatures! He's truly amazing!

126
00:10:13,110 --> 00:10:20,110
We're flattered to be serving such an inspiring leader! Captain Buggy was meant to conquer this world!

127
00:10:21,110 --> 00:10:28,110
Now, stupidest gargle! Why couldn't he just stay in his shell? Are you trying to get Whitebeard to kill me? Thanks, snail!

128
00:10:29,110 --> 00:10:31,110
Okay, let's try again!

129
00:10:32,110 --> 00:10:35,110
Start by making a declaration to conquer the world, whenever you're ready!

130
00:10:36,110 --> 00:10:38,110
Alright, you got this!

131
00:10:38,110 --> 00:10:40,110
Cue smoke! Lights are ready!

132
00:10:40,110 --> 00:10:41,110
Start rolling, you guys!

133
00:10:41,110 --> 00:10:47,110
Well, crap! No backing out now! Here goes nothing, I guess!

134
00:10:48,110 --> 00:10:54,110
Right! Come on! We're starting the broadcast! And make sure you capture the moment that I kill Whitebeard!

135
00:10:54,110 --> 00:10:56,110
Cause that's totally gonna happen!

136
00:10:59,110 --> 00:11:00,110
Hey! Look!

137
00:11:00,110 --> 00:11:01,110
It's back!

138
00:11:02,110 --> 00:11:04,110
But what's going on? I can't make out anything through that smoke!

139
00:11:05,110 --> 00:11:08,110
So did the Navy beat the pirates? Whitebeard? And Ace?

140
00:11:08,110 --> 00:11:10,110
Uh, no!

141
00:11:11,110 --> 00:11:12,110
Transponder snail! Go down a little!

142
00:11:13,110 --> 00:11:14,110
No!

143
00:11:15,110 --> 00:11:19,110
Why, hello everybody! Time for Captain Buggy!

144
00:11:20,110 --> 00:11:21,110
Whoa!

145
00:11:22,110 --> 00:11:23,110
This guy again?

146
00:11:24,110 --> 00:11:25,110
Get to the sea! Now!

147
00:11:26,110 --> 00:11:29,110
Hurry up and get on the ships! We gotta make it back to the new world and fast!

148
00:11:29,110 --> 00:11:34,110
Don't let them get away! Kill as many pirates as you can!

149
00:11:35,110 --> 00:11:38,110
I'm the only pirate you should be worrying about!

150
00:11:43,110 --> 00:11:44,110
Commander Joseph!

151
00:11:44,110 --> 00:11:47,110
He's in pretty bad shape, but I think he can make it!

152
00:11:47,110 --> 00:11:50,110
First, we gotta get him out of here to safety! Everyone lift!

153
00:11:52,110 --> 00:11:55,110
Hey, Pleinheim! Get over here! On the double!

154
00:11:58,110 --> 00:12:01,110
Hurry, straw boy! It's time to make an exit! On the double!

155
00:12:01,110 --> 00:12:04,110
Ace, let's go! The old guy made up his mind!

156
00:12:04,110 --> 00:12:06,110
The old guy made up his mind!

157
00:12:11,110 --> 00:12:13,110
I know... this is it!

158
00:12:15,110 --> 00:12:17,110
Back off, you bastard!

159
00:12:17,110 --> 00:12:18,110
You bastard!

160
00:12:47,110 --> 00:12:48,110
Back off, you bastard!

161
00:13:05,110 --> 00:13:08,110
The time for words has passed, my son!

162
00:13:08,110 --> 00:13:18,350
But tell me one last thing.

163
00:13:22,290 --> 00:13:26,210
Are you happy to have this old fool as your father?

164
00:13:32,210 --> 00:13:34,010
You got some fight left.

165
00:13:34,010 --> 00:13:38,450
Look, I'm not going to kill you today, all right?

166
00:13:39,270 --> 00:13:42,610
Don't fight it. You're too valuable to die in a place like this.

167
00:13:42,770 --> 00:13:45,290
Run wild with us and our flag will be yours.

168
00:13:46,570 --> 00:13:48,710
And I will call you my son.

169
00:13:58,110 --> 00:13:59,990
Of course, Dad!

170
00:14:04,010 --> 00:14:33,990
I will call you my son.

171
00:14:34,010 --> 00:14:39,150
Hey, what happened?

172
00:14:39,670 --> 00:14:41,690
The scaffold was destroyed.

173
00:14:41,930 --> 00:14:42,930
They're in the plaza.

174
00:14:43,150 --> 00:14:44,930
Was Fire Fist Ace executed?

175
00:14:45,310 --> 00:14:46,330
Please say something.

176
00:14:46,710 --> 00:14:48,470
Shift the camera to Whitebeard.

177
00:14:48,730 --> 00:14:50,850
I'm Captain Buggy, a legend.

178
00:14:52,370 --> 00:14:54,490
Tell us, Captain Buggy the Clown.

179
00:14:54,810 --> 00:14:58,010
Is it true you're going to be your fellow legend, Captain Whitebeard?

180
00:14:58,010 --> 00:15:03,870
And will you loudly proclaim your stake as one of the four emperors by carrying the severed head of your victim?

181
00:15:04,690 --> 00:15:06,890
I'm Captain Buggy, a legend.

182
00:15:07,690 --> 00:15:09,570
Hey, say something else.

183
00:15:10,850 --> 00:15:13,930
They got that part already to change it up a little.

184
00:15:14,810 --> 00:15:16,110
Enough with Buggy.

185
00:15:16,110 --> 00:15:18,570
Show us what's happening at Marineford.

186
00:15:18,770 --> 00:15:19,290
Yeah!

187
00:15:19,690 --> 00:15:20,230
Come on.

188
00:15:20,410 --> 00:15:21,810
Who cares about this weirdo?

189
00:15:21,950 --> 00:15:22,870
Get him out of the way.

190
00:15:22,870 --> 00:15:25,110
Okay, use that filter.

191
00:15:25,470 --> 00:15:26,010
Nice!

192
00:15:26,370 --> 00:15:26,830
There he is.

193
00:15:27,250 --> 00:15:28,630
What's he doing now?

194
00:15:28,990 --> 00:15:29,530
Out there!

195
00:15:29,530 --> 00:15:30,310
We can't see!

196
00:15:32,030 --> 00:15:33,130
Keep it up!

197
00:15:33,350 --> 00:15:34,550
We're almost there!

198
00:15:37,410 --> 00:15:38,050
Ace!

199
00:15:38,330 --> 00:15:38,810
Loopy!

200
00:15:39,150 --> 00:15:40,210
Stay in front!

201
00:15:40,330 --> 00:15:40,610
Huh?

202
00:15:40,610 --> 00:15:43,490
They're specifically targeting you two!

203
00:15:44,010 --> 00:15:46,210
We cannot let the old man waste his life!

204
00:15:46,430 --> 00:15:48,010
He will not fall in vain!

205
00:15:48,670 --> 00:15:49,350
Farewell.

206
00:15:51,470 --> 00:15:53,370
We've stolen the Navy ship!

207
00:15:53,750 --> 00:15:54,350
Hop aboard!

208
00:15:59,770 --> 00:16:03,110
Do they really think they stand a chance of escaping?

209
00:16:03,530 --> 00:16:04,290
How naive.

210
00:16:05,130 --> 00:16:06,250
Admiral Sakazaki!

211
00:16:07,070 --> 00:16:08,030
Move aside.

212
00:16:08,150 --> 00:16:09,210
I'll handle this.

213
00:16:10,610 --> 00:16:20,570
Never mind that.

214
00:16:20,730 --> 00:16:22,990
Just don't stop running until you reach the ship.

215
00:16:25,950 --> 00:16:29,490
As soon as they rescued Firefist Ace, they fled.

216
00:16:29,690 --> 00:16:31,090
What a cowardly crew.

217
00:16:31,270 --> 00:16:33,010
Just like their washed-up captain.

218
00:16:33,670 --> 00:16:34,190
What?

219
00:16:34,570 --> 00:16:36,230
He's trying to get you riled up!

220
00:16:36,290 --> 00:16:36,890
Don't listen!

221
00:16:37,310 --> 00:16:38,030
Keep it moving!

222
00:16:38,450 --> 00:16:40,350
Don't fall into his trap, you hear me?

223
00:16:40,830 --> 00:16:41,310
Yeah.

224
00:16:41,550 --> 00:16:42,870
That old man, huh?

225
00:16:43,830 --> 00:16:45,510
Some captain he is.

226
00:16:46,390 --> 00:16:47,630
It's not your fault.

227
00:16:48,710 --> 00:16:50,010
That's just Whitebeard.

228
00:16:52,010 --> 00:16:53,770
A washed-up failure.

229
00:16:56,590 --> 00:16:57,230
Ace!

230
00:16:57,230 --> 00:17:02,890
A failure?

231
00:17:02,890 --> 00:17:11,550
Take it back, or else.

232
00:17:12,230 --> 00:17:12,650
Ace!

233
00:17:12,850 --> 00:17:13,190
No!

234
00:17:13,430 --> 00:17:13,850
Don't!

235
00:17:13,930 --> 00:17:14,850
Just keep moving!

236
00:17:14,930 --> 00:17:16,250
He can say whatever he wants.

237
00:17:16,350 --> 00:17:17,010
Let's go!

238
00:17:18,270 --> 00:17:21,250
No one gets away with Mocking Pops.

239
00:17:21,570 --> 00:17:22,170
Stop!

240
00:17:22,690 --> 00:17:23,850
Take it back.

241
00:17:23,850 --> 00:17:25,090
It's not an insult.

242
00:17:25,090 --> 00:17:26,230
It's not an insult.

243
00:17:26,350 --> 00:17:27,170
It's the truth.

244
00:17:27,630 --> 00:17:29,010
Let me tell you a story.

245
00:17:30,210 --> 00:17:35,170
Your father conquered the Grand Line, something no other pirate has ever accomplished.

246
00:17:35,850 --> 00:17:40,710
After that, he opened the door to the Great Pirate Era by sacrificing his own life.

247
00:17:40,710 --> 00:17:47,870
I hate to say it being a Navy Admiral, but he was King of the Pirates, no question.

248
00:17:47,870 --> 00:17:52,510
Keeping all that in mind, Whitebeard has failed.

249
00:17:52,510 --> 00:17:58,750
His lack of ambition meant he'd never be king of anything but you simple-minded cronies.

250
00:17:59,190 --> 00:18:03,550
Once he brainwashed enough of you into doing his dirty work, he got lazy.

251
00:18:04,470 --> 00:18:07,950
Every now and then you'll find someone who paints him as a peacekeeper.

252
00:18:08,450 --> 00:18:11,630
Start trouble here and Whitebeard will come running, they say.

253
00:18:12,210 --> 00:18:12,550
Ha!

254
00:18:13,190 --> 00:18:15,810
Empty post to keep idiots like you fearful.

255
00:18:16,310 --> 00:18:19,930
You call him hero when he's nothing but a coward.

256
00:18:19,930 --> 00:18:24,870
When Gold Roger was around, Whitebeard always had second billing.

257
00:18:25,450 --> 00:18:28,190
Yet even after Roger's death, he couldn't become king.

258
00:18:29,070 --> 00:18:30,210
So there it is.

259
00:18:30,330 --> 00:18:32,230
The tale of your father's whipping boy.

260
00:18:32,430 --> 00:18:34,030
The great failure, Whitebeard.

261
